course: dictionary
lesson: 8783
title: Shallow: not deep, and not deep in thought
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shallow means not deep. There is only a short distance from the top to the bottom. «Paddle in the shallow end of the pool» tells you the water there is not deep, so you can stand up. Shallow water is safe to paddle in, but never dive into it, because you can hit your head on the bottom.
explain: The clues in a sentence show you the meaning. «Water can be deeper than it looks» warns you that shallow water may still be hard to judge, so check before you act. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "not deep" for shallow. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
explain: Shallow has a second meaning, too. A shallow person or idea does not think about serious things. In a story, «a shallow character cares only about looks» means they care about how things look on the outside, not about what matters inside. The same word is used in both meanings, so read the clues to see which one fits.
fact: Shallow means not deep: there is only a short distance from the top to the bottom.
fact: «The shallow end» of a pool is where the water is least deep, so young swimmers paddle there.
fact: «The shallows» is a noun for the shallow parts of a sea or river.
fact: A shallow person or idea does not think about serious things or care much.
fact: Shallow breathing is quick and light. Water can be deeper than it looks, so never dive into shallow water.
exercise: «Paddle in the shallow end of the pool.» What does shallow mean here? | *Not deep | Full of fish | Very cold | Very loud
exercise: «A shallow character cares only about looks.» What does shallow suggest? | Lives near the sea | Tells the truth every time | *Does not think about serious things | Always wears a hat
exercise: In a river, what are the shallows? | The deep middle where the current is strongest | A fish with spines | A bridge over the water | *The shallow parts of the river
test: «Never dive into shallow water, because you can hit your head on the bottom.» Why is this a warning? | Shallow water is always dirty | The water is cold | *The bottom is close, so diving can cause injury | Divers are not allowed in the pool
test: Shallow breathing is quick and light. What does shallow breathing mean? | Under water | *Quick and light | Loud enough to hear across the room | Slow and very deep
exam: «A punt is a flat-bottomed boat pushed along with a long pole on shallow rivers.» Where is a punt pushed along? | On a motorway | On a high mountain | In a deep ocean trench | *On shallow rivers
